# Reviewable, expiring exceptions for the CI vulnerability gate. One CVE per
# line, each with: why it is a false positive or not applicable, and a
# re-check date.

# CVE-2025-59250 — com.microsoft.sqlserver:mssql-jdbc, bundled by upstream Keycloak.
# Installed 13.2.1.jre11 IS the fixed version; trivy mis-parses the ".jre11"
# qualifier and reports it as 13.2.1 < 13.2.1.jre11. Driver is never loaded
# (image is built with --db=postgres). Re-checked against 26.7.3
# (com.microsoft.sqlserver.mssql-jdbc-13.2.1.jre11.jar, same version). Re-check
# on next KC bump (added 2026-08-23; re-checked 2026-08-31).
CVE-2025-59250

# CVE-2026-75595 — io.netty:netty-handler 4.1.136.Final, bundled by upstream
# Keycloak (Quarkus/Vert.x). Fixed in 4.1.137.Final / 4.2.17.Final; no Keycloak
# release ships the fix yet (26.7.3 is current). SslClientHelloHandler falls
# back to the default SslContext on a fragmented TLS ClientHello (SNI routing
# bypass) — only exploitable when Keycloak terminates TLS itself with per-SNI
# contexts and per-SNI clientAuth=REQUIRE. Consumer runs http.httpEnabled=true,
# no tlsSecret, proxy.headers=xforwarded; TLS terminates at Cloudflare
# Tunnel/Traefik and there is no mTLS. Re-check on next KC bump
# (added 2026-09-09; re-check by 2026-10-09 if no bump).
CVE-2026-75595

# CVE-2026-84939 — org.freemarker:freemarker 2.3.32, bundled by upstream
# Keycloak. Fixed in 2.3.35 (on keycloak release/26.7, ships in 26.7.5; not in
# 26.7.3/26.7.4). Path traversal needs an attacker-controlled malformed Locale
# reaching FreeMarker's localized template lookup. Keycloak calls
# cfg.getTemplate(name, "UTF-8") with no locale (JVM default), template names
# are fixed, and user locales are forLanguageTag-parsed and matched against
# realm supportedLocales, never passed to FreeMarker. Upstream assessment: not
# vulnerable (keycloak#52888). Remove on bump to 26.7.5+ (added 2026-09-25;
# re-check by 2026-10-25 if no bump).
CVE-2026-84939

# CVE-2026-8763 — org.bouncycastle:bcprov-jdk18on 1.84, bundled by upstream
# Keycloak via the Quarkus 3.33.3.x BOM. Fixed in 1.85; no Keycloak release
# ships it (26.8/main has 1.85.2). Name-constraint bypass in
# PKIXNameConstraintValidator; BC PKIX path building is only used by the X.509
# user/client authenticators and the nginx client-cert lookup. No X.509 user
# authenticator is configured in any flow, and there is no x509cert-lookup
# SPI; the built-in clients flow keeps client-x509 as ALTERNATIVE, but with
# TLS terminated at the ingress proxy (httpEnabled=true, no tlsSecret) it
# never sees a client cert and returns attempted(). Remove when the KC base
# ships bcprov-jdk18on >= 1.85 (currently only 26.8/main via Quarkus
# 3.33.4+/3.40; 26.7.x still pins 1.84), or if X.509/mTLS is ever enabled
# (added 2026-09-25; re-check by 2026-10-25 if no bump).
CVE-2026-8763

# CVE-2026-13506 — org.bouncycastle:bcprov-jdk18on 1.84 (same jar as above).
# Fixed in 1.85. Nesting-depth DoS only on lazy ASN.1 parsing, which BC 1.84
# uses only for CRLs (CertificateFactory.engineGenerateCRL, X509CRLHolder).
# Keycloak parses CRLs only in the X.509 authenticator, with the JDK (SUN)
# CertificateFactory, not BC. Cert/PEM/x5c/JWT parsing is eager and unaffected.
# Remove when the KC base ships bcprov-jdk18on >= 1.85 (currently only
# 26.8/main via Quarkus 3.33.4+/3.40; 26.7.x still pins 1.84), or if
# X.509/CRL checking is ever enabled (added 2026-09-25; re-check by 2026-10-25
# if no bump).
CVE-2026-13506
